  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Localization project - Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By URCS having resources to cover overhead costs, the National Society be better positioned to recruit and retain staff in selected strategic positions for safeguarding resources, mobilising more resources from diversified sources and efficiently utilising and accounting for the same.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Localisation project in Uganda aims to enhance capacity of URCS to safeguard and manage existing resources; generate increased income to meet overhead costs and fulfil mandate of humanitarian services.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Localisation project will support URCS to view income and account for resources through implementing digital transformation and electronic systems. In addition, it will enable URCS to conduct feasibility study on investment options at national and branch level, including proposed interventions at Namakwa industrial park. Findings from the study will inform URCS investment options for income generating activities (IGAs), deemed a localized and sustainable source of non-ear marked income. A proportion of the funding is dedicated to URCS prioritized and unfunded/under-funded strategic positions which are deemed key to enhancing capacity for financial sustainability aspirations.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">URCS Headquarters, Kampala, Uganda</narrative>
  </description>
